# LEGACY local cron (superseded by Cloud Scheduler — see `make setup-ingestion`).
# Only needed if you want to run ingestion from your own machine instead of GCP.
#
# Install with:  crontab -e   (paste a line below)   |   Verify with:  crontab -l
# Replace /ABS/PATH/TO/REPO with the absolute path to this repo.
# cron has a minimal PATH, so also export absolute tool paths on the line.
#
# minute hour dom month dow  command
0 7 * * * MCP_PYTHON=/opt/anaconda3/envs/mcp/bin/python GCLOUD=$HOME/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud /ABS/PATH/TO/REPO/ingestion/fetch_and_push_news.sh

# --- Older option: sync a local data/ folder instead of fetching news --------
# 0 * * * * GCLOUD=$HOME/google-cloud-sdk/bin/gcloud /ABS/PATH/TO/REPO/ingestion/push_to_gcs.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS note: if the repo is under ~/Documents, cron needs "Full Disk Access".
#   System Settings -> Privacy & Security -> Full Disk Access -> add /usr/sbin/cron
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
